diff --git a/specs/state.md b/specs/state.md
index 26bd108..1e166c8 100644
--- a/specs/state.md
+++ b/specs/state.md
@@ -577,6 +577,43 @@
   Root/callee checksums, lexical checkpoint validation, and
   projection-integrity guards remain unchanged.
 
+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+`result_persistence_profile` is an optional top-level `RunState` field (additive; schema stays `2.1`).
+Absent means the historical bundle-backed persistence and the key is omitted from `state.json`.
+The only supported value is `derived_pure_replay.v1`; any other value fails closed with a
+`ValueError` naming the profile at `RunState` construction, `StateManager.initialize(...)` and load
+(a failed load never rewrites the state file). Loads never infer, backfill or upgrade the field.
+
+Selection (at state creation only): a compiled typed public `.orc` `orchestrator run`, a new root
+from `orchestrator resume --force-restart` (the source run is left byte-for-byte unchanged), and a
+fresh non-iterative child call frame whose callee bundle provenance has `frontend_kind ==
+"workflow_lisp"`. Existing roots/frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and iteration-owned frames keep
+the historical profile. A malformed existing frame (no mapping `state`) is rejected with a
+`ValueError` mentioning `existing call-frame state` before anything is written.
+
+Under the profile, each replay-eligible compiler-generated `pure_projection` (acyclic, visited at
+most once per scope, no publishes/consumes) persists success as the exact value-free shell
+`{"name","step_id","visit_count":1,"status":"completed","exit_code":0,"outcome":{"status":"completed",
+"phase":"execution","class":"completed","retryable":false},"result_storage":"derived_pure_replay.v1"}`.
+Failed and skipped rows stay full rows. Eligible nodes own no pure result bundle, no private
+lineage and no checkpoint record, and no restore binding takes its source from them. Visit and
+cursor changes are atomic state transactions (`begin_eligible_pure_visit`,
+`reuse_interrupted_eligible_pure_visit`, `settle_eligible_pure_success`,
+`settle_eligible_pure_failure`); progress is classified `unstarted`, `interrupted`,
+`derived_complete`, `durable_failure_skip` or `progress_witness_invalid`.
+
+Resume audits persisted surfaces (a value row, pure bundle, private lineage entry, checkpoint record
+or restore binding for an eligible node raises `profile_conflict`) and progress witnesses before the
+prologue, then rebuilds only the pure values the restart boundary needs into memory from durable
+leaves, without effects or writes. Failures end the run with `error.type`
+`pure_result_replay_unavailable` and `error.context.reason` one of `durable_input_missing`,
+`durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`, `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid` or
+`progress_witness_invalid`. Default resume may admit one zero-record case,
+`VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY`, when every node before the restart node is an eligible pure node;
+otherwise it fails closed with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`. A durable
+failure of an eligible pure node cannot be re-visited (one visit per scope) and resumes fail closed.
+
 ## Reusable-Call State Contract (v2.5)
 
 - Caller-visible exports
